# deps
node_modules/

# secrets / local state
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# Where uploaded files land. Anchored, because an unanchored `uploads/` also matched
# backend/src/services/uploads/ - the source of the uploads service - and four of its five
# modules were silently missing from every clone, so a fresh checkout could not start the
# server at all. A directory name is not a safe ignore pattern when code shares it.
/backend/uploads/

# build output
release/
release-fresh/
dist/
trycord-desktop/client/
# Staged from frontend/assets by scripts/copy-client.js on every build.
trycord-desktop/build/icon.png
trycord-desktop/build/icon.ico
*.zip

# runtime logs
*.log

# editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Screenshots are output, not source. This one line covers all of it; an earlier `/tests/`
# below it was hiding six source files, and the reason given - that the directory was
# output - was already handled here.
tests/browser/shots/

# .github/ is not ignored. It held four workflows - check, publish-docker,
# release-desktop and the screenshot pipeline - and none of them were tracked, so
# the project had no CI on its default branch at all: no checks on a push, no Docker
# publishing, no desktop releases. A workflow file that is not in the repository is
# a file that never runs for anyone else.
#
# publish-docker.yml is the exception and stays untracked until someone decides.
# It builds and pushes an image on *every* push to main, so tracking it would start
# publishing images for every commit from now on rather than resuming something that
# had been switched off deliberately. That is a decision about their infrastructure,
# not a cleanup - and it is the one ignore in this file that is a decision rather than
# an accident. The file is on disk and complete; tracking it is `git add -f` and a
# push, and narrowing it to tag-triggered is a two-line edit to its `on:` block.
/.github/workflows/publish-docker.yml

# shots.yml runs the screenshot suite, which is scaffolding for UI work rather than
# something every push should pay for. An earlier version of this comment said it lived
# on a shots/* branch together with the scripts it drives; there is no such branch, and
# the scripts it referenced were untracked, so the reasoning described a setup that did
# not exist. The real reason to leave it out is in backend/scripts/browser/README.md:
# a repository that ships a browser-driving workflow to every self-hoster asks each of
# them to keep a Chromium around for a test they did not ask for. The suite itself is
# tracked and runs on demand.
/.github/workflows/shots.yml

# Screenshots from backend/scripts/browser/shots.mjs. Generated on every run and
# uploaded as a CI artifact; nothing to commit.
backend/shots/

# Database dumps. They hold every user row including password hashes and email
# addresses, so they belong on the machine that made them and nowhere else. Git is not
# somewhere a copy of that goes.
/data/
